-- Band-masked attention centroid: the weighted 4D centre of everything an
-- entity attends to through a given band. This is the "general area" a concept
-- occupies, as opposed to its own coordinate, which is a function of its
-- content (the composition of its codepoints) and therefore says nothing about
-- meaning — 'dog' and its translations have unrelated coordinates by
-- construction. The centroid over a semantic band is where they converge.
--
-- BUG FIXED 2026-08-04 — this function returned NULL on every call it had ever
-- served, silently. The band filter was:
--
--     SELECT e.id FROM entities e
--     WHERE e.highway_mask IS NOT NULL
--       AND laplace_highway_mask_bits(e.highway_mask)
--           && laplace_highway_mask_bits(p_band_mask)
--
-- which asks for ENTITIES whose own highway mask overlaps the band, then joins
-- that set to consensus.type_id. But a highway mask records which bands an
-- entity has EDGES IN; it is not a statement about which band a relation type
-- BELONGS TO. That is relation_highway_bit(type_id), straight from the
-- manifest. Measured on the foundation ladder: the CTE matched 0 rows for
-- word_id('dog') against band 3, while dog demonstrably carries 8
-- IS_SYNONYM_OF edges (bit 153, band 3) and 9 HAS_SENSE (bit 112, band 3).
-- Zero rows in, NULL out, no error.
--
-- It was also a full scan of every entity (4.34M) with a set-returning
-- function evaluated per row — the per-row SRF shape the architecture rules
-- name explicitly — to produce a set that is fully determined by the manifest
-- and has at most 233 members.
--
-- The mask is expanded to its bit list ONCE, in the scalar subquery, and each
-- candidate edge is then an integer membership test against that array. No
-- entities scan, no per-row SRF.
--
-- No SET search_path: it blocks SQL inlining, which costs the planner the
-- consensus (subject_id, type_id) index path through this body. Every
-- reference is @extschema@-qualified instead. See GH #860.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION laplace_attention_centroid(
    p_entity   bytea,
    p_band_mask bytea)
RETURNS TABLE(cx float8, cy float8, cz float8, cm float8, total_weight float8)
LANGUAGE sql STABLE PARALLEL RESTRICTED AS $$
    WITH band_bits AS MATERIALIZED (
        SELECT @extschema@.laplace_highway_mask_bits(p_band_mask) AS bits
    ),
    attended AS (
        SELECT c.object_id,
               @extschema@.eff_mu(c.rating, c.rd)::float8 AS w
        FROM @extschema@.consensus c
        CROSS JOIN band_bits b
        WHERE c.subject_id = p_entity
          AND c.object_id IS NOT NULL
          AND @extschema@.relation_highway_bit(c.type_id) = ANY (b.bits)
          AND @extschema@.eff_mu(c.rating, c.rd) > 0
    ),
    weighted AS (
        SELECT w.coord, a.w
        FROM attended a
        JOIN @extschema@.v_word_points w ON w.id = a.object_id
        WHERE w.coord IS NOT NULL
    )
    SELECT
        SUM(ST_X(coord) * w) / NULLIF(SUM(w), 0),
        SUM(ST_Y(coord) * w) / NULLIF(SUM(w), 0),
        SUM(ST_Z(coord) * w) / NULLIF(SUM(w), 0),
        SUM(ST_M(coord) * w) / NULLIF(SUM(w), 0),
        SUM(w)
    FROM weighted
$$;
